{%- doc -%}
  CSS-only layout patch for templates/page.contacto.json, rendered there via a "Custom Liquid"
  block (`{% render 'contacto-page-bridge' %}`). Takes no params. `{% style %}` output isn't
  scoped to the block or section it's rendered from, so every rule is scoped through the marker
  div below instead: `:has(.contacto-layout-scope)` stands in for "the section this bridge was
  placed in". `.mionas-card` and `.mionas-contact-form` get the same scoping even though they're
  page-unique today, since both are generic Mionas components rather than page-specific classes.
{%- enddoc -%}
{%- comment -%}
  The row/column wrapping, per-column minimum widths, and the card row's 1300px breakpoint used to
  live here too, but they're now native mionas-group/mionas-card settings (wrap_children,
  min_width) set directly on the relevant blocks in page.contacto.json -- organic wrap based on
  available space, not a hardcoded viewport number. The address/day/hours nowrap rules moved the
  same way, onto each mionas-text block's own `prevent_wrap` setting. What's left below -- the
  align-items: stretch override and the form height chaining -- doesn't map to any block's
  settings.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="contacto-layout-scope" hidden></div>
{% style %}
  /* Native `vertical_alignment: center` visibly centers the two columns once they're different
     heights; `stretch` top-aligns them and grows the shorter one to match. Not expressible as a
     mionas-group setting -- the native vertical_alignment select has no "stretch" option. */
  [data-testid='section-content']:has(.contacto-layout-scope) > .group-block > .group-block-content {
    align-items: stretch;
  }

  /* Contact form grows to the column's full height (align-items: stretch above); this chain
     passes that height down through each wrapper so it lands in the message field instead of
     as blank space below the submit button. :has(textarea), not :last-child, so it still
     targets the message row if fields are ever reordered. resize: none since a manually
     resized textarea would fight the auto-grow. */
  [data-testid='section-content']:has(.contacto-layout-scope) .mionas-contact-form > form {
    height: 100%;
  }

  [data-testid='section-content']:has(.contacto-layout-scope) .mionas-contact-form > form > .mionas-form {
    flex: 1;
  }

  [data-testid='section-content']:has(.contacto-layout-scope) .mionas-contact-form .mionas-form > .mionas-contact-form__surface {
    flex: 1;
  }

  [data-testid='section-content']:has(.contacto-layout-scope) .mionas-contact-form__surface .mionas-form-field:has(textarea) {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  /* field-sizing: content grows the box with typed input past the flex-filled baseline above,
     no JS. Chromium-only for now -- Safari/Firefox just keep the static baseline height, no
     breakage. min-height keeps its own rows="5" floor even when the flex-filled baseline would
     otherwise be shorter (e.g. once the form column is short on mobile). */
  [data-testid='section-content']:has(.contacto-layout-scope) .mionas-contact-form__surface .mionas-form-field:has(textarea) textarea {
    flex: 1;
    height: 100%;
    min-height: 5lh;
    resize: none;
    field-sizing: content;
  }
{% endstyle %}
